            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-xxl",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xl",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Keeping up with filter replacement might not sound exciting, but honestly, it's one of the most important things you can do to keep your purifier working well and your air actually clean.</p><p>Here's the straightforward answer: most filters need replacing every 6 to 12 months. But the exact timing depends on what type of filter you have, how much you're running your purifier, and what's in the air around you.</p><p>Let's talk through what affects replacement timing, what to expect budget-wise, and how to get the most from every filter you buy.</p><h2>How Often Should You Replace Air Purifier Filters?</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_KnqYBR": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
