            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>The basic rule isn't complicated: standard HEPA filters last 12 months under normal conditions. Carbon filters need replacing every 3-6 months. But \"normal conditions\" are doing a lot of work here.</p><p>What really makes a difference:</p><ul><li>Where you live - High pollution areas, wildfire smoke, heavy pollen seasons all wear filters faster.</li><li>How often you run it - a 24/7 operation shortens filter life compared to occasional use.</li><li>Your household - Pets, cooking, smoking, and allergies all mean more particles in the air.</li><li>Room size match - If your purifier is undersized for the room, it works harder and filters wear faster</li></ul><p>The good news? Modern purifiers don't make you guess. Most include filter change indicators that track actual usage and air quality, not just counting days. When your filter is really saturated, not just at some arbitrary time limit, the purifier tells you.</p><h2>Air Purifier Filter Lifespan by Type</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_qy8nHW": {
          "type": "image_caption",
