            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Different filters do different jobs, which is why they have different replacement schedules.</p><h3>HEPA Filters (6-12 months)</h3><p>These capture particles down to 0.3 microns, including dust, pollen, pet dander, and mold spores. Most need replacing once a year under normal use. Heavy dust, pet hair, or poor air quality might mean replacement every 6-9 months.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/blueair-performance\">Blueair models capture even smaller particles down to 0.1 microns</a>, which means more thorough cleaning and longer-lasting effectiveness compared to standard HEPA alone.</p><h3>Carbon Filters (3-6 months)</h3><p>These remove odors and gases by absorbing them into carbon pores. Once those pores fill up, they're done. You can't recharge them.</p><p>Homes with pets or cooking smells often replace these every 3 months. Less active use in clean conditions? They might last closer to 6 months.</p><h3>Pre-Filters (Washable, every 2-4 weeks)</h3><p>These catch the big stuff, hair, lint, dust, before it reaches your main filter. Clean them every 2-4 weeks by vacuuming or gently rinsing with water.</p><p>Let them dry completely before reinstalling. Here's why this matters: regular pre-filter cleaning is one of the easiest ways to extend your HEPA filter life by several months.</p><h2>Annual Air Purifier Filter Replacement Costs</h2><p>Here's where budgeting comes in. Annual filter costs typically run $50-$200, depending on your purifier model and how often you replace filters.</p><p>Realistic annual costs by room size:</p><ul><li>Small room units (up to 200 sq ft): $50-$100/year</li><li>Medium room units (200-400 sq ft): $100-$150/year</li><li>Large room units (400+ sq ft): $150-$300/year</li></ul><p>If you run 24/7, add electricity (roughly $20-$50/year, less than running a standard light bulb).</p><p>Your total annual cost? Usually $100-$250. That's genuinely not much for breathing cleaner air every single day.</p><h2>How to Save Money on Air Purifier Filter Replacements</h2><h3>Set up automatic filter subscriptions</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/subscribe\">Blueair's filter subscriptions save upto 15%</a> with automatic delivery. Set it and forget it, cleaner air and lower costs.</p><h3>Buy pre-filter multi-packs</h3><p>Some retailers offer 10-20% off when you buy several filters at once. Stock up during sales.</p><h3>Clean pre-filters consistently</h3><p>This single habit can extend your HEPA filter life by months. It takes 5 minutes and saves real money.</p><h3>Adjust usage for air quality</h3><p>When outside air is clean, run your purifier on a lower speed. You still get good air quality while reducing filter wear.</p><h3>Use genuine filters</h3><p>Cheap third-party filters might save $10 now, but they don't maintain your purifier's performance and might void your warranty. Genuine filters keep everything working as designed.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/collections/air-purifier-filters\">Find genuine replacement filters that match your Blueair purifier's specifications</a> to maintain optimal performance and protect your investment.</p><h2>Signs Your Air Purifier Filter Needs Replacement</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_Q8DrHF": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
