        "text_e9yarP": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-lg",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-lg",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Your purifier's indicator light will tell you. But you can also check yourself.</p><p>Visual inspection clues:</p><ul><li>The filter looks dark gray or black.</li><li>Dust comes out when you gently tap it.</li><li>Visible buildup or discoloration</li></ul><p>Performance warning signs:</p><ul><li>Airflow drops even at high speed.</li><li>Your purifier is running louder than usual.</li><li>Odors linger when they used to disappear.</li><li>Allergy symptoms returning or worsening.</li></ul><p>When you see these signs, replacement time has come.</p><h2>What Happens When You Don't Replace Air Purifier Filters on Time</h2><p>Here's the real cost of delaying replacement: you pay more money for worse results.</p><p>A saturated filter forces your motor to work harder, pulling more electricity while delivering less clean air. You're paying more for worse performance. Plus, a clogged filter stops trapping particles effectively and actually starts recirculating them back into your room.</p><p>For families with allergies, asthma, or young children, poor air quality often leads to:</p><ul><li>More doctor visits</li><li>Missed work or school</li><li>Disrupted sleep</li><li>Worsening respiratory symptoms</li></ul><p>The cost of proper filter maintenance is honestly small compared to dealing with those consequences.</p><h2>Getting the Most From Your Air Purifier Filters</h2><p>Simple maintenance keeps everything running efficiently and your costs reasonable:</p><p>✓ Clean pre-filters regularly (every 2-4 weeks)</p><p>✓ Replace filters on schedule (follow the indicator light)</p><p>✓ Use genuine filters that match your purifier</p><p>✓ Run at appropriate speeds for the current air quality</p><p><a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/collections/air-purifier-filters\">Set up automatic filter delivery with Blueair</a> to save both money and the hassle of remembering to order.</p><p>Your family deserves to breathe well at home. Staying on top of this one simple task keeps your investment working exactly as designed.</p><h3>FAQs</h3><p><strong>Q. How long do Blueair filters actually last?</strong></p><p>6-12 months, depending on usage and air quality. The smart indicators in your purifier track your specific usage, so you get alerted when your filter, not some generic timeline, needs replacing.</p><p><strong>Q. Can I wash and reuse HEPA or carbon filters?</strong></p><p>No. Washing damages the fiber structure that traps particles. Only pre-filters are washable. Always check your manufacturer's instructions.</p><p><strong>Q. Are expensive filters really worth the cost?</strong></p><p>Yes. Quality filters maintain your purifier's performance level and keep your warranty valid. Cheap filters often don't fit properly and can reduce effectiveness. You're protecting your investment.</p><p><strong>Q. What's my total annual cost for an air purifier?</strong></p><p>Electricity (24/7 operation): $20-$50</p><p>Filter replacement: $100-$200</p><p>Total: roughly $120-$250 per year for clean air around the clock.</p><p><strong>Q. What if I delay replacement for an air purifier?</strong></p><p>Your purifier works harder, uses more energy, runs louder, and stops cleaning effectively. You lose the main benefit of having a purifier.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        }
      },
